## 5. Validation scripts (`package.json`)

```json
"validate:okf": "tsx scripts/validate-okf.ts",
"validate:content": "tsx scripts/validate-content.ts"
```
- `scripts/validate-okf.ts` — walks all `.md`/`.mdx` (excluding `node_modules/.next/.source/out/.git`, `.claude/skills/`, `.agents/skills/`, `.sandcastle/`, README.md, and a few named exempt files) and fails if any file lacks a frontmatter block or has an empty/missing `type` field. This is OKF v0.2's one required key — `maerkte/idee-kontakt-begegnungen.mdx` and `index.mdx` already satisfy it (`type: Article` / `type: Overview`).
- `scripts/validate-content.ts` — walks `src/content/docs`, checking: every `<Illu>`/`<Slide>` `slug=` used in MDX resolves in `src/data/illus.json`/`slides.json`; every `illus.json`/`slides.json` image path resolves under `public/`; every non-separator `meta.json` `pages` entry resolves to a real `.mdx`/`.md` file or subfolder; every relative markdown link/image path resolves to a real file. Both `maerkte/meta.json` pages (`index`, `idee-kontakt-begegnungen`) already resolve fine today.
