## Review Findings

**Hard violations:** None found. OKF `type` is present and non-empty in all 4 files (Overview/Article/Note). The Ansatz tagline in `index.mdx` (`**_Innovation aus Tradition, die ersten Weichen sind gestellt._**`) matches the glossary's Märkte row verbatim. Status flips to `stable` are consistent with the all-stable convention already used across `annaeherung/`.

**Judgement-call smells / structural deviations:**

1. **`kontakt-und-begegnung.mdx` — novel `type: Note`.** Every other page across all migrated Xeniapolis districts (annaeherung, kontexte, etc.) uses only `Overview` or `Article`. Introducing a third type for a single one-off page is a **Mysterious Name**-adjacent smell (Fowler) — the type isn't defined or explained anywhere, and readers/tooling have no precedent for what `Note` means vs. `Article`. Judgement call: harmless today (OKF only requires non-empty), but risks **Speculative Generality** if no other "Note" pages ever appear, or **Divergent Change** pressure later if a real taxonomy has to be retrofitted.

2. **`index.mdx` — truncated Ansatz section vs. sibling structure.** `annaeherung/index.mdx`'s `## Ansatz` section has the bold tagline *plus* a second explanatory sentence ("Muster für die Anlage und Gestaltung..."). The new `maerkte/index.mdx` Ansatz section has only the bold tagline, jumping straight to `## Gestaltungsschwerpunkt`. This is a judgement call — may simply reflect a shorter source page — but it's a structural inconsistency with the precedent set by item 4 (annaeherung).

3. **`kontakt-und-begegnung.mdx` prose describing the five planned features** ("Das Gästebuch der Wissensstadt Xenia", "Der Xenia-Tribune", etc.) reads as a paraphrase/summary rather than a flagged verbatim quote. Per `docs/how-to/transcribe-xeniapolis-source.md`, this is fine if treated as authored explanatory prose (not a transcription) — but if these five names were lifted from the original page's literal wording, they should either be quoted exactly with `[sic]` on anything unusual, or clearly framed as paraphrase. Flagging as a judgement call since I can't verify against the actual 1990s source page from the diff alone — not a confirmed hard violation.

No Duplicated Code, Feature Envy, Data Clumps, Shotgun Surgery, Message Chains, Middle Man, or Refused Bequest observed; the diff is small and self-contained. `meta.json`'s pre-existing `title`/`description` ("Märkte" / generic placeholder) weren't touched by this diff and mirror the same placeholder pattern in `annaeherung/meta.json`, so not flagged.
